  "output": "(1) Bug: `reapOrphanedRuns` defaults `staleThresholdMs` to `0`, so `cutoff = Date.now() - 0 = now`, and `lastHeartbeatAt <= cutoff` treats every in-flight run as stale.\n\n(2) Clean restart calls `reapOrphanedRuns()` with no arg, so every still-`running` run has `lastHeartbeatAt <= now` and is permanently `failRun(..., 'process_lost')` (no retry).\n\n(3) Fix: default a positive staleness window (e.g. minutes), and only fail when `lastHeartbeatAt <= Date.now() - threshold` with `threshold > 0`; do not reap with `0` on startup\u2014resume/requeue fresh runs instead.",
